From c8479bd5c3edd26cd7e6ebd33decde82278e6ce0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 07:25:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] game panes: an overlay that can read the pane

Layer 0 could only go underneath, because a function that draws from its
own coordinates and nothing else cannot filter anything. A second slot
now runs over the finished pane and is handed it:

    float3 background(pane p)
    float4 overlay(float4 colour, pane p)

with p.colour(at) and p.smooth(at) for the picture, p.index(at) for the
raw palette index and p.palette(i) for a colour. That is the whole of
what a filter needs, so heat haze, reflection, bloom, aberration and
curvature stop being things the host has to offer as options and become
the program's own business. Still nothing else is reachable: not the
pool at large, not another pane, not the host.

It is `overlay` and not `filter` because MSL already has metal::filter,
the sampler enumeration, and the two are ambiguous at the call site.

Retro's overlay raises heat off the ground, bleeds the bright pixels and
drops the light at the corners; 4 turns it on and off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0109-game-panes-an-overlay-that-can-read-the-pane.patch 11646f97e5d8a9f523cfdfb939f63030110279d2f6c501cae6a99a173e1487ad
